      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Here's a revised version of the professional wording for the kitchen staff:\n\n\"Dear Catering Team,\n\nWe have a number of guests with severe nut allergies and a significant number of vegans attending the gala. To ensure their safety and comfort, please review the menu and identify any nut-containing dishes that need to be labeled as such. Additionally, please ensure that all vegan options are clearly labeled as such.\n\nTo minimize the risk of cross-contamination, please follow these guidelines:\n\n* Use separate utensils, cutting boards, and preparation surfaces for nut-free and nut-containing dishes.\n* Label all dishes with ingredients used, including nuts and any allergens.\n* Clearly indicate which dishes are vegan-friendly.\n* Provide a separate list of ingredients for guests with severe allergies to review before serving themselves.\n\nYour attention to these details will help us provide a safe and enjoyable dining experience for all our guests.\n\nBest regards, [Your Name]\"\n\nI hope this revised version meets your needs!",
